      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pat the chicken pieces completely dry with kitchen paper. Mix the cornflour, plain flour, black pepper, and garlic together. Toss the chicken in the flour mixture to coat evenly. Shake off any excess. Rest on a wire rack for 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the vegetable oil in a deep, heavy pot to 170C. Fry the chicken in batches for 8 to 10 minutes until cooked through but only lightly golden. The internal temperature should reach 74C. Remove and drain on a rack."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Increase the oil temperature to 190C. Return the chicken and fry again in batches for 3 to 4 minutes until deep golden and very crisp. Drain on a rack."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make your chosen sauce. For the soy-garlic glaze: combine all ingredients in a small saucepan and simmer for 3 minutes until slightly thickened. For the spicy sauce: combine gochujang, sugar, and rice vinegar and warm gently."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Toss the hot chicken in the sauce immediately before serving. Scatter sesame seeds over the top. Serve at once."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Coating is falling off during frying",
              "fix": "The chicken was not dry enough before coating. Pat it completely dry and let the coated chicken rest for at least 30 minutes before the first fry."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Chicken is not crispy after the second fry",
              "fix": "The oil was not hot enough for the second fry. Use a thermometer and wait until the oil reaches 190C before adding the chicken."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Coating goes soft quickly after adding the sauce",
              "fix": "Add the sauce at the very last moment and serve immediately. The cornflour crust stays crisper for longer than a flour-only coating."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Korean fried chicken is everywhere in Korea. It is a late-night favourite eaten with beer, a combination so popular it has its own nickname. It is ordered for delivery, eaten at street stalls, and made at home for weekends. The dish became internationally popular through Korean television and food culture in the early 2000s."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
